# A run that ends one column before the margin (six columns: a, then two pairs,
# leaving column 5 free), the next write landing in that column; then a run that
# ends exactly at the margin (three pairs) arms the deferred wrap, so an ASCII
# byte after it starts the next row.
a\xE4\xB8\xAD\xE6\x96\x87b\r\n\xE4\xB8\xAD\xE6\x96\x87\xE6\xB5\x8Bc
